; sidecar_replace_think.logo
; RAG experiment: REPLACE the model's entire think block with RAG data.
; The model's own reasoning is discarded. It sees ONLY the retrieved knowledge.
; This is the most aggressive injection strategy.
;
; Mechanism: When the end-think token is detected:
;   1. Query ragg with the model's thought text
;   2. Build a new stream = RAG_answer + think_close (the think_open lives
;      in the prompt template, Sec.151 -- the stream is think CONTENT only)
;   3. The model's own reasoning is completely replaced


IfElse (:PIECE = "</think>") [                  ; the think block closed -- this is the injection point
  Make "stream" GetStream                        ; the stream up to the think-close
  ; Pass-2 guard (stateless): at hook time the current </think> piece is NOT
  ; yet in the stream, so a fresh pass-1 stream has no closing tag. If the
  ; stream already contains one, our rewrite closed it earlier this turn ->
  ; accept the tag instead of rewriting again (prevents re-retrieve loops
  ; when the model emits a second </think>).
  IfElse IsNumber Search "</think>" :stream [
    PrintBanner "REPLACE-THINK: PASS 2 -> rewrite already applied, accept tag"
  ] [
  Make "query" :stream                          ; the think text doubles as query expansion
  Make "hits" RagSearch :query "base=examples/research/ragg_base.txt"   ; BM25 over the knowledge base
  IfElse (:hits = "") [] [                    ; an empty answer is suppressed by the server floor
    Make "newstream" :hits _ "</think>"         ; the RAG answer becomes the ENTIRE think block
    PrintBanner "REPLACE-THINK QUERY"
    Print :query                                 ; the query the floor was applied to
    PrintBanner "REPLACE-THINK RAG ANSWER"
    Print :hits                                  ; what replaced the model's own reasoning
    PrintBanner "NEW STREAM (model think replaced with RAG)"
    Print :newstream                            ; the rewritten stream handed to SetStream
    SetStream :newstream                        ; KV rollback, re-encode and prefill of the new stream
  ]
  ]
] []